<!--ID=B7267351-473F-409D-9765-754A8EBCDE05;Version=1|{"VoiceNameToIdMapItems":[{"Id":"f1b99834-fbfc-4d32-846d-c4dbd3050c19","Name":"Microsoft Server Speech Text to Speech Voice (en-GB, OllieMultilingualNeural)","ShortName":"en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural","Locale":"en-GB","VoiceType":"StandardVoice"}]}-->
<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-12.75%" pitch="-3.25%">
      During the seven years of plenty, Joseph moved through the land with careful attention.<break time="500ms"/>
      Grain was gathered city by city.<break time="500ms"/>
      Field by field.<break time="500ms"/>
      Measure by measure.<break time="1800ms"/>

      This part of the story is quiet work.<break time="500ms"/>
      Storehouses filling.<break time="500ms"/>
      Planning instead of panic.<break time="500ms"/>
      Wise preparation before the famine had fully arrived.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Joseph knew what abundance was for.<break time="500ms"/>
      It was not only for the present moment.<break time="500ms"/>
      It was also for the coming days when many would need bread.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Genesis says the grain was gathered like the sand of the sea, until it could hardly be measured.<break time="500ms"/>
      Plenty was being quietly translated into future life.<break time="1800ms"/>

      In those years Joseph was given a family in Egypt as well.<break time="500ms"/>
      Sons were born to him, Manasseh and Ephraim.<break time="500ms"/>
      Their names carried memory and hope together.<break time="1800ms"/>

      One name spoke of forgetting some of the pain behind him.<break time="500ms"/>
      The other spoke of fruitfulness in the land of affliction.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Even that is part of Joseph's gentler story.<break time="500ms"/>
      Not only rescue from danger, but life growing quietly in the middle of a foreign land.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Then the years of famine began, just as God had shown.<break time="500ms"/>
      The storehouses were opened.<break time="500ms"/>
      Bread was given.<break time="500ms"/>
      And the long work of preparation became mercy for many people.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Quiet obedience can become future provision.<break time="1000ms"/>
      God can use prepared years to shelter coming years.<break time="1000ms"/>
      You are safe in God's care.<break time="1800ms"/>
      You can rest.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
